      "message": "This is one of those areas where the Android cppstyle and Google cppstyle differ.  For Android, these names should be push(), pop(), and empty(), and since underscores are only used for extern \"C\" function names, the internal versions would be something like pushImpl()/popImpl() or pushInternal()/popInternal() or whatever else feels best to you, rather than _Push()/_Pop().  (This will also be more consistent with the rest of the file.)\n\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1QivJI_03TcfRAyMGWkTNHEdiQh8h_F-rYGup9soSeLA/edit#heading\u003dh.92cudhmf3aa5",
